1
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,860
Excuse me. Is this seat taken?

2
00:00:15,860 --> 00:00:17,350
No, it's not taken.

3
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:18,500
Oh, thank you.

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:20,050
Oh, let me help you with this.

5
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:26,600
Oh, thank you.

6
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,780
Do you want to sit by the window?

7
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,710
No, no, no. I like the aisle seat better.

8
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:39,340
Please, you sit by the window.

9
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,380
My name is Stewart... Malcolm Stewart.

10
00:00:41,380 --> 00:00:42,380
Pleased to meet you.

11
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:50,590
I'm Elsa Tobin. How do you do?

12
00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:52,630
Do you live in New York?

13
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:55,090
No, no. I'm from Florida.

14
00:00:55,090 --> 00:01:00,210
I am, too. But didn't you just get on?

15
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:02,720
No, no. I just changed my seat.

16
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:04,690
A man next to me was smoking,

17
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:10,410
and smoke really bothers me.

18
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:12,420
Where are you from in Florida?

19
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:15,040
Titusville. It's near Orlando.

20
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,340
Small world. I'm from Titusville, too.

21
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:21,270
Really? What part?

22
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:24,110
My husband and I live near Spaceport.

23
00:01:24,110 --> 00:01:26,670
I know that area.

24
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:31,810
My house is only a few miles from Spaceport.

25
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:32,890
Do you still live there?

26
00:01:32,890 --> 00:01:35,390
Oh yes, yes. My husband's there now.

27
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:41,630
He couldn't take time off to come to New York with me.

28
00:01:41,630 --> 00:01:43,520
Do you still live there?

29
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:49,670
No. I sold the house and the furniture,

30
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:53,870
put a few personal things in an old trunk,

31
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:56,730
and shipped it to my children in New York.

32
00:01:56,730 --> 00:01:58,900
That's my destination.

33
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:00,670
Are you married?

34
00:02:00,670 --> 00:02:04,650
My wife died four years ago.

35
00:02:04,650 --> 00:02:08,750
She was a wonderful woman. A real friend.

36
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:14,000
I'm sorry. Really, I'm sorry.

37
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,040
Lots of wonderful memories.

38
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:19,110
We were married almost fifty years.

39
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:21,970
Well, forty-seven, to be exact.

40
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:25,280
John and I celebrate our fortieth anniversary next month.

41
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:30,800
Oh, congratulations! That's nice.

42
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,560
What does John do?

43
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,670
He's an aerospace engineer

44
00:02:34,670 --> 00:02:38,020
and works for Orlando Aircraft Corporation.

45
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:42,880
He started with them almost forty years ago.

46
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:44,950
What do you do?

47
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:49,880
I just retired. Had my own company.

48
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:56,620
A construction company. Roads, bridges, big stuff.

49
00:02:56,620 --> 00:03:04,140
But I just sold it and retired.

50
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:09,660
Excuse me, ma'am. Ticket, please.

51
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:13,560
Would you kindly hold these keys, please?

52
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:16,100
I have a ticket, I know.

53
00:03:16,100 --> 00:03:17,990
I was in the smoking section.

54
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:21,270
It's OK, lady. Take your time.

55
00:03:21,270 --> 00:03:24,020
I'm sure it's in your purse, Mrs.Tobin.

56
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:29,430
Oh, here it is.

57
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:31,580
And here are your keys.

58
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:38,280
Thank you.

59
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,390
Do you have family in New York?

60
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:46,120
No, no. But I do have very close friends in New York City.

61
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:49,420
We like to go to the theater together.

62
00:03:49,420 --> 00:03:51,040
You said you have family in New York.

63
00:03:51,040 --> 00:03:53,130
Yes, indeed.

64
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:57,130
A son and his wife and their three children-

65
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,460
my grandchildren.

66
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,600
You must be excited.

67
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:04,010
I can't wait, to see them!

68
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,440
Are you going to live with them?

69
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:06,230
Yes.

70
00:04:06,230 --> 00:04:08,280
Permanently?

71
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:12,310
Well... they want me to,

72
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,820
but it's too early to know for sure.

73
00:04:14,820 --> 00:04:17,520
I'm pretty independent.

74
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:22,410
I tried to teach my kids the importance of independence,

75
00:04:22,410 --> 00:04:27,850
but I'm not sure I want to be alone.

76
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:32,950
Some people don't mind being alone. I do.

77
00:04:32,950 --> 00:04:36,960
I understand. But tell me.

78
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:39,920
Why did you stop working?

79
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:48,590
I retired because... I wanted to be with my family.

80
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:51,590
I didn't want to be alone anymore!
